 "note": "Quick, Draw! rhinoceros 5621907212730368, facing left. Stroke 0 is the two horns drawn as one zigzag. Stroke 1 is the head: the snout point and chin at the left, the face line up to the brow, and a large round outline that also covers the shoulders. Stroke 2 is the body, a second round outline behind the head. Strokes 4 and 5 are the front legs and strokes 6 and 3 the hind legs, each a short line. The rig carries the body by the shoulder and rump points. The head and horns turn together at the neck toward the nose point, so the nose dips to the grass and swings as the rhinoceros grazes. Each leg swings at its top as the rhinoceros shifts its feet.",
